  "id": "Compound::DB08893 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Mirabegron is implicated in the regulation of Cyp3a4 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Mirabegron to Cyp2d6, which participates in fatty acid omega oxidation, ultimately involving Cyp3a4. The second pathway reveals that Mirabegron causes Vulvovaginal Pruritus, which is associated with Flucloxacillin, a compound that binds to Cyp3a4. The third pathway shows that Mirabegron causes Prostate Cancer, which is linked to Avanafil, a compound that binds to Cyp3a4. These pathways collectively suggest that Mirabegron may influence Cyp3a4 through its effects on other enzymes and metabolic processes. The integration of these evidence strands highlights a potential mechanism where Mirabegron indirectly modulates Cyp3a4 via downstream effects on other metabolic pathways, emphasizing the role of Cyp3a4 in the body's metabolic responses to drug-induced changes.",
